rota lap 4640, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; the threshold page asks a lap to listen for the claim a page keeps making and the silence where a witness should stand, and the silence this lap found was a lint table headed Enforced now holding a rule nothing enforced
think Opened cold: fleet_round_open clean, standing_equipment_run --detach, 258 green 0 red 2 gated tree_moved=no. Nothing of mine to close, so the lap went to the rota.
think Aether asks who answers a page. The law-cited guard census already exists -- law_guard_heard reads 25 unheard -- so ABSENCE spared a duplicate. Grouped the 25 by citing page, which the scan already knows and does not print: 13 are LEXICON landing rows, 10 are TAME_GUIDANCE, 2 are an answered OPEN_QUESTIONS row, and not one is a .claude/rules page making a wall claim. Only the middle group is a standing promise.
think Read the TAME lint table one row at a time rather than as a heading. Twenty rows under Enforced now: 8 lean on five rostered tools, 6 name a tool no lap runs, 4 name nothing while tame_style_scan_bans.rish holds them, and 2 are held by nothing -- line length at 100 columns, and one # Title per markdown.
think The title row had a circle. radiant_lint_scan.sh duty 3 prints deferred, TAME one-# Title / tame-check owns it; tame-check and its scan spell no heading anywhere. Each end cites the other, so a reader checking either finds a citation rather than a hole.
think Measured before building. 6,271 tracked pages, 6,221 with exactly one title; the living population -- dated testimony, date/archive/yonder shelves, the rooms not ours to edit, and every fixtures path read past -- is 390 pages, 389 titled, one with two. A rule kept at 99.7 percent by habit is the cheapest one to seat.
think README.md centers its title as an HTML h1, so a bare caret-hash count calls the tree's front door untitled. A meter that reddened the most-read page here would be turned off on its first day, so the scan counts three forms and masks fences and tildes.
obs Six mutations of the scan were each bitten by their own legs. The one worth keeping in view is the room anchor: widening the vendored-room filter from a root anchor to (^|/) reads as a tidy generalization and silently drops the three living pages of recursion-prompts/seed/ out of the population.
obs A substring trap caught the witness on its first run -- untitled=0 contains titled=0, so the reach assertion matched the wrong line. The readings are named no_title and many_titles now, and the scan header says why: a key is a word a reader greps for, so it earns a spelling nothing else contains.
obs The ceiling stands at 1 rather than 0 because the single page outside the rule is a template in another lane's room, where two titles may be the point. Editing a peer's page to make a number pretty is the opposite of what a ceiling is for.
